# Dark Phoenix — Cursor AI Rules

## Project Overview
This is the Dark Phoenix AI video clipping platform.
- Frontend: Next.js 15, TypeScript, Tailwind, Shadcn UI, Prisma, Auth.js, Inngest, Stripe
- Backend: Python, Modal (GPU), WhisperX, Gemini API, ffmpeg, boto3, AWS S3

## Core Rules
- Preserve existing architecture — make targeted changes only, no big refactors
- Never commit secrets — all keys go in .env or Modal secrets
- No SQLite — database is Supabase Postgres via Prisma
- YouTube download must be server-side using yt-dlp, never in the browser
- Watermark text is "unartch" burned via ffmpeg drawtext filter into the MP4 file
- Output format: 9:16 vertical, captions + watermark in every final clip

## Key Files to Understand Before Changing
- ai-podcast-clipper-backend/main.py — Modal GPU worker, clip rendering
- ai-podcast-clipper-frontend/src/inngest/functions.ts — job queue
- ai-podcast-clipper-frontend/src/actions/s3.ts — S3 upload/download
- ai-podcast-clipper-frontend/src/actions/generation.ts — clip signed URLs
- ai-podcast-clipper-frontend/src/components/dashboard-client.tsx — main UI

## What Needs to Be Built
1. YouTube URL ingestion (server-side yt-dlp download → S3 upload)
2. unartch watermark burned into every clip via ffmpeg drawtext
3. Google Drive upload of final clips
4. Deploy frontend to Vercel, backend to Modal

